2026-02-11 00:21:02,682 - DocumentGraderNode - INFO: Retrieved document What Is Volatility, Mathematically?

Volatility is a statistical measure of the dispersion of data around its mean over a certain period of time. It is calculated as the standard deviation multiplied by the square root of the number of time periods, T. In finance, it represents this dispersion of market prices, on an annualized basis. is relevant
